    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d573">

                <pb facs="0762" n="638" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg638"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.1931/45½</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Secretary of State of a Conversation
                        with the Panaman Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Alfaro</hi>), <hi
                        rendition="#italic">January 4, 1923</hi></head>
                <dateline>
                    <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-head" calendar="gregorian"
                        type="conversation-or-meeting-date" when="1923-01-04">January 4, 1923</date>
                </dateline>
                <p>The Minister left a long note with the Secretary<anchor n="2" xml:id="d573-f1"/>
                    and explained orally that he did so to set forth the position of the Government
                    of Panama in relation to negotiations which were about to begin for the purpose
                    of making a treaty to take the place of the Taft Agreement. The Minister
                    explained that his Government was desirous of approaching the matter in the most
                    friendly and conciliatory spirit. The Secretary said that the matter of the
                    abrogation of the Taft Agreement was before Congress, and that as soon as it had
                    been abrogated so as to open the way for negotiations this Government would be
                    pleased to take the matter up with Panama. He was gratified at the statement
                    made by the Minister and could assure him that this Government desired to deal
                    with the matter in the same friendly spirit.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
